{
  "name": "329. Fork deployment switches: provider job accounting off and passthrough heartbeat off (provider error fixture, job accounting switch)",
  "description": "Local fixture regression for TXE-6519 (Bifrost–Tokun contract C3 and C11), no live provider calls. Start tests/e2e/api/runners/provider-error-fixture.mjs, start an isolated gateway on tests/e2e/api/provider_config/provider-error-fixture.config.json, which sets client.disable_provider_job_accounting and client.disable_passthrough_sse_heartbeat and the harness's default setup token, and run with providerErrorFixture=1; every case is skipped otherwise. 329.1 reads both switches back through GET /api/config. 329.3 and 329.4 create a video task and a batch through the gateway; the fixture answers in OpenAI shape, keeps the video complete on retrieve and the batch in progress, and counts every call under a fixed key. 329.5 reads the fixture's counters at once and again after 70 seconds, longer than the batch sweeper's one-minute tick and the video sweeper's 30-second tick: only the creates (and the JSONL upload an inline batch makes) reached the fixture, so Bifrost made no vendor call of its own between requests. 329.6 to 329.9 show the video's retrieve, download and delete (the fork's cancel; TXE-6521 adds POST /v1/videos/{id}/cancel) still work with no provider job record, each reaching the fixture exactly once. 329.10 streams a passthrough chat completion whose vendor pauses 2.5 seconds between events, longer than the one-second heartbeat interval, and 329.11 compares the bytes the caller read with the bytes the fixture sent (GET /__sent). Red before the switches existed: 329.1 reported no switch, the video sweeper polled GET /v1/videos/{id} within 60 seconds, and the passthrough body carried ': heartbeat' lines.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "329.1 openai fixture gateway reads both fork switches back through GET /api/config (job accounting switch)",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "var j = pm.response.json();",
              "pm.test('disable_provider_job_accounting reads back on', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(j.client_config && j.client_config.disable_provider_job_accounting, pm.response.text().slice(0, 400)).to.equal(true);",
              "});",
              "pm.test('disable_passthrough_sse_heartbeat reads back on', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(j.client_config && j.client_config.disable_passthrough_sse_heartbeat, pm.response.text().slice(0, 400)).to.equal(true);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "X-Bifrost-Setup-Token",
            "value": "bifrost-e2e-setup-token"
          }
        ],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/config",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "api",
            "config"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "329.2 fixture hit counters reset before the openai job accounting rows",
      "event": [
